From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:35:39 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] ngp-screen

The Neo Geo Pocket gets its own Screen section, listed after PlayStation
and shown only when the card holds NGP games, with two rows. Shader
walks Off, LCD3x (exact 3x, the Game Gear precedent) and the shared
retro list, stored in Config/ngp_shader.txt; the in-game Shader row and
the shader shortcut walk the same list. Picture is Actual by default,
then Stretch, with no Crop because the NGP has no overscan, stored as
ngp in Config/picture.txt. There is no PAL Speed row: the core runs at
60.25 fps and there is no PAL NGP.

Actual draws the 240x160 canvas at 3x, so the 160x152 picture is 480x456
in the middle of the panel. Stretch fills the 720x480 panel with the
picture alone, both ways.

The Screen page follows nelynes/slotPlus a8eae4c and stretching both ways
follows 1ef7226 (GPL-3.0), reimplemented.
